androidx - cargo-apk2 (build Android APKs straight from Termux), git repo ~/dev/androidx
  SETUP.md = full guide, README.md = quickstart, tools/, examples/hello-apk
  git clone https://github.com/mzdk100/cargo-apk2 ~/dev/cargo-apk2
  cargo install --path ~/dev/cargo-apk2/cargo-apk2
  ~/dev/androidx/tools/setup-sdk.sh  # idempotent, builds ~/Android/sdk
  .bashrc gets: ANDROID_HOME, ANDROID_NDK_ROOT, JAVA_HOME (java-21-openjdk)
  apk needs: pkg install aapt aapt2 d8 apksigner openjdk-21 android-tools
  no real NDK for aarch64 -> setup-sdk.sh fakes the SDK+NDK (symlinks Termux
  clang/llvm binutils, google platform-36 android.jar, and a python `zipalign`
  shim because Termux ships none); builds must set
  build_targets = ["aarch64-linux-android"] or rely on the same host triple
  rollback: pkg uninstall aapt aapt2 d8 openjdk-21 android-tools
            rm -rf ~/Android/sdk ~/dev/cargo-apk2 ~/dev/androidx
            rm -f ~/.cargo/bin/cargo-apk2 ~/.android/debug.keystore
            drop the cargo-apk2 block from .bashrc
            NOTE: `pkg upgrade abseil-cpp` ran to unbreak adb and pulled
            abseil-cpp 20260817, imagemagick 7.1.2.34, mpv 0.41.0-5 - not undoable
  test app: ~/dev/androidx/examples/hello-apk -> target/debug/apk/hello-apk.apk

